"wikipediaTitle":"Kurile Lake","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Kurile_lake.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a2/Kurile_lake.jpg","w":1200,"h":809,"author":"Игорь Шпиленок","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurile_lake.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_mutnovsky","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Mutnovsky","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":52.453,"lng":158.195},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_mutnovsky","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":5,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":308,"wikidataSitelinks":22,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["mutnovsky","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Mutnovsky is an active complex volcano located in the southern part of Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia, approximately 75-80 km south of Petropavlovsk-Kamchatsky. The volcano is formed from several cones and lava flows from flank eruptions that have merged into a single massif.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Mutnovsky","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Mutnovka2.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2b/Mutnovka2.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Денис Анисимов at ru.wikipedia","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mutnovka2.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_vilyuchik","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Vilyuchik","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":52.70556,"lng":158.2775},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_vilyuchik","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":6,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":350,"wikidataSitelinks":20,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["vilyuchik","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Vilyuchik, also known as Vilyuchinsky i