anic caldera located in the eastern part of Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia. Together with the Geyzernaya caldera it hosts the largest geothermal field in the Kamchatka Peninsula.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Uzon"},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_kambalny","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Kambalny","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":51.3,"lng":156.86667},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_kambalny","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":164,"wikidataSitelinks":17,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["kambalnykamchatkakrai","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Kambalny is a stratovolcano located in the southern part of the Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia. It is the southernmost active volcano of Kamchatka. It has erupted mafic rocks. It has a summit crater as well as five cinder cones on its flanks which are the source of lava flows.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Kambalny","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Kambalny.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fe/Kambalny.jpg","w":1200,"h":703,"author":"Игорь Шпиленок","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kambalny.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_ksudach","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Ksudach","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":51.81667,"lng":157.53333},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_ksudach","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":1,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":140,"wikidataSitelinks":19,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["ksudachkamchatkakrai","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Ksudach is a stratovolcano in southern Kamchatka, Russia. The last eruption of Ksudach was in March 1907, on or around 28 March, which was one of the largest ever recorded in Kamchatka with a Volcanic Explosivity Index of 5. The summit area comprises overlapping calderas.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Ksudach","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/KsudachVolcano_ISS009-E-16836.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/KsudachVolcano_ISS009-E-16836.jpg","w":1200,"h":1200,"author":"Earth Observations Laboratory, Johnson Space Center.","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KsudachVolcano_ISS009-E-16836.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_akademia_nauk","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Akademia Nauk","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":53.96667,"lng":159.45},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_akademia_nauk","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":153,"wikidataSitelinks":25,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["akademianauk","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Akademia Nauk is a volcano located in the southern part of Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia, next to the stratovolcano of Karymsky. The volcano is filled with a few calderas, and the most notable one is known as Karymsky Lake.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Akademia Nauk"},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_lake_kronotskoye","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Lake Kronotskoye","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":54.78639,"lng":160.22667},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_lake_kronotskoye","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":139,"wikidataSitelinks":25,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["lakekronotskoye","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Lake Kronotskoye is a triangle-shaped lake located in Kamchatka Krai, Russia, 30 kilometres (19 mi) north of the Valley of Geysers and 40 kilometres (25 mi) away from the east coast of the Kamchatka Peninsula.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Lake Kronotskoye","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Lake_Kronotzkoe.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Lake_Kronotzkoe.jpg","w":1200,"h":787,"author":"Игорь Шпиленок","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Kronotzkoe.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_zhupanovsky","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Zhupanovsky","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":53.59,"lng":159.3147},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_zhupanovsky","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":96,"wikidataSitelinks":19,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-25"},"hashtags":["zhupanovskykamchatkakrai","kamchatkakrai"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Zhupanovsky is a volcanic massif located in the southeastern part of the Kamchatka Peninsula, Russia. It consists of four overlapping stratovolcanoes. After 54 years of inactivity, the volcano began erupting on 23 October 2013 and again in 2014, continuing nonstop into 2016.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Zhupanovsky","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Zhupanovsky_volcano.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/56/Zhupanovsky_volcano.jpg","w":1200,"h":798,"author":"Игорь Шпиленок","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhupanovsky_volcano.jpg"}},{"id":"kamchatka_krai_asacha","areaId":"kamchatka_krai","name":"Asacha","category":"viewpoint","tags":["mountains","views","hiking"],"location":{"lat":52.355,"lng":157.827},"visitMinutes":180,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"kamchatka_krai_asacha","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":60,"wikidataSitelinks":18,"fetchedAt